WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
Every OSINT workflow should start with a clear intelligence requirement:

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.060
the question the work must answer for a named decision or operational need.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.740
A vague request such as research this company invites uncontrolled searching.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.130
A useful requirement identifies the subject, timeframe, decision,

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.320
and required level of confidence.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.500
Identify who needs the answer and how it will be used.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.420
An incident responder may need a rapid assessment within an hour.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.050
A due-diligence team may accept a longer timeline but require documented primary sources.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.860
Audience and consequence determine depth, format, review, and escalation.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.300
Define scope explicitly.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.360
In-scope elements may include public infrastructure, official records,

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.535
or published statements within a date range.

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:39.890
Out-of-scope elements may include personal data unrelated to the purpose,

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.815
private accounts, restricted systems,

00:00:41.815 --> 00:00:45.156
or activity requiring legal authority that the team does not possess.

00:00:45.156 --> 00:00:49.360
Record constraints such as deadline, language, geography, approved tools, budget,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.085
privacy rules, and retention.

00:00:51.085 --> 00:00:53.340
State assumptions and terms that could be ambiguous.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.365
A clear definition of the entity prevents records from different people or organizations

00:00:57.365 --> 00:00:59.185
with similar names from being merged.

00:00:59.185 --> 00:01:01.620
Specify what a satisfactory answer looks like.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.980
This may include confirmed findings, assessed possibilities, important gaps,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.561
and recommended validation.

00:01:06.561 --> 00:01:10.060
Set stopping conditions so the team can conclude when the question has been answered to

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:13.770
the required level or when available public information is insufficient.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.580
Requirements can change as evidence appears,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.860
but changes should be documented and approved.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.802
This preserves accountability and prevents quiet expansion into unrelated collection.

00:01:21.802 --> 00:01:24.960
The requirement remains the anchor for deciding whether each search, source,

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.840
and reported detail is necessary.
